WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/vehicles/components/telemetry-panels/InfoTile.tsx — a PURE presentational tile:
    GlassPanel(p-4, overflow-hidden) →
       label row[ <Icon h-3.5 w-3.5 shrink-0> + <span truncate>{label}</span> ]  (text-muted, text-xs, mb-1.5)
       value   <p class="text-lg font-semibold truncate" title={String(display)}>{display}</p>   (color, default text-primary)
       sub?    <p class="text-[10px] text-muted mt-0.5">{sub}</p>
    display = (typeof value === 'boolean') ? (value ? 'Yes' : 'No') : value
    props   : icon, label:string, value:string|number|boolean, color?:string (default text-[var(--text-primary)]), sub?:string
  No data hooks. The prompt records "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)" and "Charts/maps: (none)".
  No loading/empty/error/stale/offline branches exist in the source — those belong to whatever data the *caller*
  feeds the tile (the same disposition prompt 0010 ToolCard recorded for the other pure-presentational surface).
  The ONLY hardcoded literals the web source carries are the boolean display words 'Yes' / 'No'.
  The single web call site (telemetry-panels/TelemetryGrid.tsx) confirms the live color palette:
    text-emerald-300 (success), text-amber-300 (warning), text-rose-300 (danger), text-[var(--text-muted)], default primary.

